From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] tolerate objext detection failure in PHP 4.1/4.2 configure

PHP 4.1 and 4.2 bundle a libtool configure macro whose object-suffix
check fails on Apple Silicon (arm-apple-darwin24) even though the compiler
check immediately before it succeeds. The build only ever produces .o
files on these platforms; skip the fragile probe instead of aborting.
---
 a/configure | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1 +1 @@
-  { echo "configure: error: installation or configuration problem; compiler does not work" 1>&2; exit 1; }
+  ac_cv_objext=o
@@ -1 +1,2 @@
-OBJEXT=$ac_cv_objext
+ac_cv_objext=o
+OBJEXT=$ac_cv_objext
@@ -68257,5 +68257,5 @@
   else
-    { echo "configure: error: installation or configuration problem: compiler cannot create executables." 1>&2; exit 1; }
+    ac_cv_exeext=no
   fi
   rm -f conftest*
   test x"${ac_cv_exeext}" = x && ac_cv_exeext=no
-- 
2.47.1

